cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, data or trained models, please cite this repository."
title: "PorScaDB-ML: predicting DFT HOMO-LUMO gaps of porphyrinoids and benchmarking scaffold extrapolation"
abstract: >-
  A machine-learning pipeline that predicts DFT HOMO-LUMO gaps of porphyrinoid
  macrocycles from 2D descriptors and RDKit fingerprints, together with a
  controlled benchmark of ten regressors across three data-splitting axes
  (random, meso-substituent, macrocyclic scaffold) and two feature sets.
authors:
  - family-names: "Zhang"
    given-names: "Chengwei"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - porphyrinoid
  - HOMO-LUMO gap
  - molecular descriptors
  - scaffold split
  - extrapolation
  - SHAP
  - scikit-learn
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Laughableomputers/PorScaDB-ML"
